Original commit body from c9e96f2014a83729e982096f9688fbf5c6e7475f:

Rust declared ZERO module_completeness entries, so no rust module could ever be
an examined negative and every clean rust boundary verdict was withheld. This
lands 20 grants over 33 audited modules, making rust the second of the fifteen
shipped catalogues to declare any (python has 76; the other thirteen are still
at zero).

A grant asserts that EVERY I/O primitive a module exposes is catalogued, so a
wrong one manufactures a false all-clear. The probe never grants: it left 18
candidates and each was adjudicated against the installed toolchain's source.

A DEFAULT TYPE PARAMETER CAN CARRY A BOUNDARY. std::collections::HashMap came
back with no signal, yet HashMap::new() returns HashMap<K, V, RandomState> and
RandomState's initialiser calls sys::random::hashmap_random_keys — an OS
entropy read, invisible to a text scan of map.rs because RandomState is defined
in another module. It keeps the grant on cross-language consistency, not
judgement: python already grants secrets, random and uuid on the recorded
reasoning that OS-RNG seeding belongs to the row of the module that PERFORMS it
(os.urandom), and os.getrandom was removed from env_read outright because "a
CSPRNG read is not an environment read under any reading" — this vocabulary has
no kind for entropy at all. A test pins that dependency.

Thirteen modules are deliberately refused, `std` itself foremost: granting the
whole standard library would turn every unmatched std call into an examined
negative. The clock modules are refused for the opposite reason to the rest —
WI-pavob ruled a clock read IS host_info_read, so they need rows (WI-tubij),
not a no-I/O declaration.

Measured A/B over rust repos, both arms, fresh cache each: no verdict flips,
because the surviving inconclusives are held by rungs UPSTREAM of the module
list (method-starvation on std::path::Path; languages with no catalogue at
all). But the grants are not inert — rage's unadjudicable-module count falls
33 -> 25, and the residual is third-party crates, which are out of catalogue
scope by standing ruling. A gate-level positive control pins the mechanism
directly, because "no verdict moved" cannot by itself tell a working grant
blocked upstream from a grant that does nothing.

Also corrects two docstrings this falsifies: a test fixture that justified its
empty completeness map as "rust.yaml's real state", and an io_boundary.py
sentence counting "13 of the 14 shipped catalogues" when there are fifteen.

